ng Leaders Program Liberty Partnership Program Local Things to do Campus Events Calendar Support Network Center for Multicultural Affairs Counseling Services Department of Spiritual Life and Service First Year Experience Health Services Information Technology International Student Services ROTC Campus Safety Title IX and Title VI Student Conduct Related Links Science and Health Initiative University Announcement Bookstore Commencement Academic Calendar President's Report Lecture Series Marist Italy Sustainability Dean's List Related Links Science and Health Initiative University Announcement Bookstore Commencement Academic Calendar President's Report Lecture Series Marist Italy Sustainability Dean's List Campus Life Residence Life Dining Athletics Office of Community and Belonging Campus Map Marist ID & Marist Money Get Involved Student Organizations and Clubs Club Sports Intramurals and Recreation Murray Student Center Emerging Leaders Program Liberty Partnership Program Local Things to do Campus Events Calendar Support Network Center for Multicultural Affairs Counseling Services Department of Spiritual Life and Service First Year Experience Health Services Information Technology International Student Services ROTC Campus Safety Title IX and Title VI Student Conduct Athletics Image of Marist university student in the Center for Career Services office. Center for Career Services Unlock Your Professional Potential Image of redbackground with script M. Destination: Success. Choosing a career path is a process that unfolds throughout the college years and beyond. It involves discovering individual potential, learning about career fields, and gaining career-related experience in high-quality organizations. The Center for Career Services offers a variety of programs and information to assist students and alumni with setting career goals. Watch Video Watch Video Make a Gift > 94 % EMPLOYED OR IN GRAD SCHOOL 94% of Marist graduates are employed or attending graduate school within six months of graduation. TOP 50 \"COLLEGES THAT CREATE FUTURES\" Marist is consistently ranked among The Princeton Review’s Top 50 “Colleges That Create Futures.” A + BEST ACADEMIC REPUTATION The U.S. Department of State’s Bureau of Educational and Cultural Affairs recently identified Marist as a \"U.S. Student Top Producer.\" ↑ ↑ LEADING CHANGE AT TOP COMPANIES Our grads work at industry leaders like Amazon, JP Morgan Chase and Co., Google, Paramount+, and Microsoft. Handshake Career and Internship Database Career Resources for Students Resources for Employee Recruitment Career Courses and Digital Resources Career Events Scholarships and Fellowships If it weren’t for the excellent Career Services Office at Marist College and the wonderful professors and mentors I have had throughout my time as an undergraduate, I would not be where I am today. Jennamichelle Merolla Ad Sales, NBC Universal Looking back on my time at Marist, the support I received from professors, the Career Center, SGA advisors, and friends has been exceptional. These are professionals/mentors who genuinely care about your well-being. Roda A. Mohamed Investment Banking Analyst, Goldman Sachs Marist’s staff and faculty’s dedication and investment in my growth and learning were instrumental in helping me find a job I love and grow the confidence required to navigate the corporate world for the first time. Through continuous emails about opportunities, networking events, resume workshops, etc., I was able to explore a myriad of career paths and understand what aligned with my interests. Genesis Batista Lopez Compliance Risk Consultant, KPMG My professors at Marist stressed soft skills just as much as technical skills and made the effort to build teacher-student relationships that extend beyond class sessions and semesters. With the help of my professors, my technical skills and networking put my foot in the door for many opportunities. Nicholas Mays Associate Consultant, Microsoft When the time came to think about my future, Career Services was instrumental in helping me throughout the job searching and interview process. They were my cheerleaders and incredibly supportive in making me feel as though the sky was the limit. Natalie Garcia Associate Producer, DailyMailTV Start Your Career with Confidence Equipped with a Marist degree and a network of more than 50,000 Red Fox alumni, you’ll enter the workforce with confidence, knowing that your resume is supported by not just strong academics, but also valuable experiences in the field. Outcomes Archive > Download the PDF Outcomes Brochure 2026 image of marist \"m\" in red. Connecting Students with Alumni at Paramount Headquarters Marist students from across all disciplines visited Paramount's headquarters in Manhattan for a Road to the Workplace trip, where they toured the entertainment company's offices, attended an alumni panel discussion, and even sat on the iconic Forrest Gump bench—all part of a dynamic day of networking and discovering how Red Fox connections can open doors in the entertainment industry. Read More Red Fox Ready for the Real World Uncover Your Career Interests We’ll facilitate assessments and help you find for-credit career exploration courses . Qualify for Internship Funding We’ll help you apply for financial support where internship experiences are often unpaid or underpaid. Make Alumni Connections We work with the Marist Alumni-Student Network to connect current student and recent graduates with alumni who are established in their field. Explore the Job Market We source literature about current and emerging career trends . Prepare for your Job Hunt We’ll help you create a thorough job search plan and identify potential employers. Pursue Fellowships and Graduate Study We support you one-on-one through applications , entrance exams, and registration. Download the PDF Center for Career Services Contact Us Asset Publisher Featured News Marist University Launches Empire State Promise to Expand College Choice for New York Families Eligible families earning $200,000 or less will pay no more than $32,000 for tuition, housing, and dining when enrolling at Marist in 2027. Read More MBA Program Named Among Nation’s Top 50 Online Programs The Princeton Review recognized Marist's Online MBA for its academic excellence, innovative curriculum, and strong student satisfaction. Read More Marist University Recognized as One of The 15 Best Colleges in U.S. Preparing Students for AI Economy Marist was just named one of The 15 Colleges Best Preparing Students for the AI Economy, alongside Dartmouth, MIT, Ohio State and other top-tier institutions, according to Town & Country magazine and college counselors at IvyWise. Read More View More Get More Info Loading... Your Path to Success Choosing a career path is a process that unfolds throughout the college years and beyond. It involves discovering individual potential, learning about career fields, and gaining career-related experience in high-quality organizations. The Center for Career Services offers a variety of programs and information to assist students and alumni with setting career goals and seeking employment. Handshake - Additional Resource to Search for Jobs and Internships Click here for Login Link Employers, please register in Handshake here to post jobs and internships for Marist students. Schedule an Appointment With a Career Coach How Can We Help? Courses/Services Career Events For Employers For Students Career Services Career Services Available to Students and Alumni Career Resources : Our team offers books, pamphlets, digital materials, and other resources describing career fields, employment outlook, and emerging career trends. We also offer FOCUS 2, a computer-assisted guidance program with an occupations and graduate school database. The Marist Alumni Career Network assists current students in finding out about the career fields through conversations with alumni. Career Assessment : Career assessment for students includes inspiring self-assessment, enhancing career decision-making skills, and honing interest identification. Pre-Professional and Graduate School Advisement : For students looking into pre-professional and graduate school programs, we spend one-on-one time with individual students assisting with school choices, applications, entrance examinations and studying, preparation of registration materials, as well as our annual Graduate School Forum. Career Courses : Marist University offers a number of career courses designed to help students in all stages of their collegiate experience to pursue their ideal career path. Job Search Preparation : Our team assists in resume development, cover letter writing, interview preparation, and job research skills. We help students create a thorough job search plan and identify potential employers. Employment Services : We offer internship and career opportunities, job-hunting directories, brochures, and employer information. Our team organizes on-campus interviews, as well as the Fall and Spring Career and Internship Fairs, which have had great success in pairing students with the perfect post-graduation internship or job. Internship Funding : The Presidential Internship Scholarship assists students with financial needs to secure internships in fields and locations where such experiences are often unpaid or underpaid. Click here to review deadlines and submit your application. Students & Alumni Employers Managers Hidden Close footer Join the Conversation Instagram Facebook LinkedIn TikTok YouTube Twitter Academics Experiental Learning Majors, Minors, and Programs Study Abroad Athletics Clubs and Activities Dining Residence Life Quick Links Directory Visit Campus Maps & Directions Careers at Marist Support Marist Marist 100 - Strategic Plan Website Feedback Newsroom Virtual Tour To view an accessible version of our virtual tour, click here. Marist University, 3399 North Road, Poughkeepsie, NY 12601 | 845-575-3000 © Copyright 2026 \n                    Marist University. All Rights Reserved. Disclaimers | Privacy Policy | Accessibility Policy | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information For screen reader problems with this website, please email helpdesk@marist.edu Close"
